  <div class="section no-top-padding"><div class="container"><div class="hero4 hero-content-centered"><div class="subtitle">January 21, 2023</div><h1>A self-guided tour itinerary of the area surrounding Hotel Toile Blanche in Vence, French Riviera.</h1></div></div></div><div class="full-frame-image-wrapper" style='background-image:url("https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/639af6c370637a84eae3b0bb/63de6bb7cc6c48b99b2fc016_nighthawk-shoots-kH4U4sn3qt4-unsplash.jpg")'></div><div class="section"><div class="container"><div class="blog-post w-richtext"><ol role="list"><li>Start your tour at the Fondation Maeght, a modern art museum featuring works by famous artists such as Joan Miro and Marc Chagall. Allow at least an hour to fully appreciate the collection.</li><li>After visiting the Fondation Maeght, walk to the Matisse Chapel. This small chapel features a series of colorful mosaics created by Henri Matisse. Allow 20-30 minutes to fully take in the art.</li><li>Next, take a hike on the Sentier des Douaniers, a coastal hiking trail that offers breathtaking views of the Mediterranean Sea. Allow at least an hour for this hike.</li><li>After your hike, have lunch at Le Toile Blanche, the hotel's restaurant, which serves a variety of traditional Provencal dishes made with fresh, locally sourced ingredients.</li><li>After lunch, take a stroll through the charming town center of Vence. The Place du Grand Jardin is a lovely spot to relax and take in the sights and sounds of the town.</li><li>Lastly, visit the Saint-Paul de Vence, a fortified medieval village, is also nearby and definitely worth a visit. Allow at least an hour to explore the village and its history.</li></ol><p>Please note that this is an approximate itinerary and the time spent at each location can vary depending on your interests and pace</p><h5>‍</h5><p>‍</p></div></div></div><div class="section no-top-padding"><div class="container"><div class="heading-wrapper inner-spacing div-block"><h2>Continue reading</h2></div></div><div class="container no-padding-mobile"><div class="blog-collection-list-wrapper w-dyn-list"><div class="blog-flex-thirds w-dyn-items" role="list"><div class="blog-item w-dyn-item" role="listitem"><a class="collection-link-block w-inline-block" href="best-places-to-eat-the-tastiest-local-food-around-toile-blanche.html"><div class="collection-image-wrapper"><img alt="Best places to eat the tastiest local food around Toile Blanche" class="image-cover" loading="lazy" sizes="100vw" src="/assets/images/page-img-0bd0acfefc8c5b.jpg"/></div><div class="collection-content-wrapper"><div class="subtitle">Best places to eat the tastiest local food around Toile Blanche</div><img alt="" class="collection-arrow-img" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/page-img-a926ac09f8f7bc.svg"/></div></a></div><div class="blog-item w-dyn-item" role="listitem"><a class="collection-link-block w-inline-block" href="tings-to-do-around-toile-blanche.html"><div class="collection-image-wrapper"><img alt="Things to do around Toile Blanche" class="image-cover" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/page-img-28965838c96078.jpg"/></div><div class="collection-content-wrapper"><div class="subtitle">Things to do around Toile Blanche</div><img alt="" class="collection-arrow-img" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/page-img-a926ac09f8f7bc.svg"/></div></a></div><div class="blog-item w-dyn-item" role="listitem"><a class="collection-link-block w-inline-block" href="10-best-swimmig-holes.html"><div class="collection-image-wrapper"><img alt="10 Best Swimming Holes at (and around) Toile Blanche" class="image-cover" loading="lazy" sizes="100vw" src="/assets/images/page-img-0bd0acfefc8c5b.jpg"/></div><div class="collection-content-wrapper"><div class="subtitle">10 Best Swimming Holes at (and around) Toile Blanche</div><img alt="" class="collection-arrow-img" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/page-img-a926ac09f8f7bc.svg"/></div></a></div></div></div></div></div>

